errors.Is(err, doc.ErrEmpty) { return nil } on validate.Report's
fmt.Errorf(Join(title, body)). At run time only doc.ErrNoTitle can come back: a
report holding doc.ErrEmpty always matches. The Join may hold nil for either
operand, so the check is undecided for the whole value and, by design (plan P07:
a guard removes only what is proven), both leaves stay, marked possibly handled
("wrapped value may be nil"). Expected: doc.ErrNoTitle present; doc.ErrEmpty at
most possibly handled, never unmarked.
